meta {
  name: create-table
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/admin/v1/tables
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "label": "Patio 9",
    "seats": 4
  }
}

tests {
  test("responds 201, or 409 if the label is taken", function () {
    expect([201, 409]).to.include(res.status)
  })
}

docs {
  # Add a table

The QR token is generated server-side with 160 bits of entropy. It is not a database key but a
capability, so it is sized to be unguessable rather than merely unique (docs/DECISIONS.md D4).
}
